From 87b6834dec53fcbfb3f1527690589c220a9b3b9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:50:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): a jstack task held for your go or your accept,
 launched or not, unfolds why with read and approve or read and accept

jbus's work.json names the word that lifts a row in `lift` (approve, accept) and why it holds in `why`, so the tree reads both and keeps no rule of its own. A launched task whose brief changed after the go shows the lines that changed, and Approve sends the go for the sha the user read; a pull request jmerge holds for --accept gets Accept the same way.
